  "data_rules": {
    "availability": "At D(T) = 23:00 Europe/Lisbon the signal and the EUR conversion use only values already published: Xetra close (17:30 CET), ECB reference rate (~16:00 CET) and US close (16:00 New York), all earlier than D(T) on every day. Fills happen at the asset's next close.",
    "cash": "EONIA - 0.085 p.p. until 2019-09-30, EUR STR from 2019-10-01, minus 0.25 p.p., ACT/360, negative rates kept; interest from T-1 to T uses the rate for T-1.",
    "data_end": "Last complete session before the snapshot; later rows are ignored.",
    "eur_conversion": "USD series are divided by the ECB USD-per-EUR reference rate of the same date, or the latest earlier one; more than 4 weekdays of staleness fails closed.",
    "master_calendar": "Union of the universe assets' provider rows.",
    "sessions": "An asset's sessions are the provider's rows. Exchange-calendar differences are listed by the audit; a calendar session without a provider row is no session for that asset (its move is captured by the next row).",
    "ter": "TER accrues per calendar day (TER / 365). An own series contains the product TER; a US ETF proxy contains its own TER and is adjusted by (TER_us - TER_eu) / 365 per calendar day. Scenario zero adds back the TER the series contains; double deducts one more TER_eu.",
    "total_return": "Daily factor (close_t + dividend_t) / close_{t-1}; split-adjusted close; dividends gross at the ex-date, reinvested at that close. The provider's Adj Close is used only to verify the data."
  },
